{
 "about": "Catalog hosts for the front-page check (catalog-store/frontPageCheck.js; owner decision, 23 November 2026: \"You can check yourself\"). flagged: hosts whose robots.txt allows every agent (*), and so the app, but blocks AI agents, so no agent may look for a bot wall (mostly Koha and Aspen at ByWater). polaris-literal: Polaris PowerPAC hosts whose robots.txt disallows only the capital-P /Polaris/search/ path, which a case-sensitive reading (RFC 9309, owner decision of 23 November 2026) does not apply to the lowercase /polaris/ catalog. From the US national catalog survey and the open research of 23 November 2026; families and systems as that survey found them. The app's own server asks each host for its front page once, as MyBookshelf/1.0, after its robots.txt allows it, with no search. Added 24 November 2026 (USA plan step 4, Koha): every catalog host the US Koha entries in server/data/us-catalogs.json use, including Koha hosts in ByWater's zone known only from DNS leads (robots.txt not read; ByWater's Cloudflare-managed file is assumed) and the Aspen Discovery fronts of entries whose Koha host is not known, so each has its result when its identity is settled. A connected entry on one of these hosts is offered only once its result shows the host open (server/services/directory.js). unseen: hosts whose robots.txt allows Claude agents too, or was not read, but which no agent was cleared to contact (Metro Library System's Grove-hosted Aspen Discovery; the TLC hosts connected by the coordinator's DNS-lead decision of 24 November 2026), so a wall is unknown. Added 24 November 2026 (USA plan step 5, Aspen Discovery): every host a connected or waiting US Aspen entry uses (Greenville's excepted: agents may look there and saw no wall), and the TLC DNS-lead hosts. Added 24 November 2026 (USA plan step 6, Polaris PowerPAC): every host a connected or waiting US Polaris entry uses where no agent looked for a wall (polaris-literal for the vendor template; unseen for Henderson, Longview and New Orleans's candidate hosts, which have no robots.txt but no agent was cleared to contact); the hosts whose robots.txt also blocks the lowercase /polaris/ (Onondaga, Valley Library Consortium, San Bernardino County) are left out, as class D, and Richland's catalog is listed by its own name (catalog.richlandlibrary.com). wall-seen: hosts whose catalog showed a bot wall to a research agent (Nashville, Orange County FL, SWAN) or, at the app's launch, to the app's own requests (CLEVNET, MAIN); the app's own check decides (coordinator decision, 24 November 2026). Added 24 November 2026 (USA plan step 7, Apollo): the <name>.biblionix.com hosts of the connected and waiting Apollo entries that no agent was cleared to contact (unseen: Rolling Hills, Killeen); Clear Lake's and Lawton's are not here (agents may look there and saw no wall), nor, from 24 November 2026, Brownsville's, Horseshoe Bend's (Idaho), Anderson County's, Gilford's, Lamar County's and Orange City's (an agent read each catalog page once and saw no wall). Georgia PINES (gapines.org, USA plan step 8) is not here either: the app checks it through the OpenSRF gateway, which an agent read without a wall, and the app has used since October 2026. tools/directory/apollo-hosts.mjs adds the host of every later Apollo entry here unless an agent saw it without a wall. memberLists: shared catalogs whose members are only estimated or unknown, read once for the catalog's own member or location list (frontPageCheck.js). catalogLinks: waiting libraries whose homepage URL is in the evidence, read once for their outgoing catalog links and title. skipped: the waiting ones not covered, and why.",
